[{:db/id "q-327582/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "eb08e1a4-a8fe-55c1-bada-3af804afeb6f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327582/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "5b30bb6a-8c03-5ced-8485-0efaf0f09acd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327582/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "4f571752-b187-5cc7-be16-f65ef9631918" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327582/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "9185aeb7-090f-56ae-89d4-2ef1ea157c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327582/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "901518f3-ebc4-5fde-b49f-0f566cfbf1ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327582/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6932dcd8-556f-58b4-8016-a859ae830847" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-327582/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-327582/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-327582/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-327582/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-327582/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-327582/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327582" :question/id #uuid "fb2e0b5a-2f3a-5be5-b507-1b0c071903a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-327582" :question/problem "Consider the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nfor some function $f(x,y).$ The table below shows the intermediate quantities computed in the first iteration of the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |\n\nGiven that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{4},$ at which of the following points is the function $f$ evaluated during this iteration?\n\n- $(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{2})$\n- $(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{4})$\n- $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{8})$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c\n$$\n\nthe increment in $y$ using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method with step size $Δx$ is computed as the weighted average of four sample slopes:\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{′}=f(x,y)$ is the estimated slope at the initial point $(x,y),$\n\n- ${y}_{1}^{′}=f({x}_{1},{y}_{1})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{2}^{′}=f({x}_{2},{y}_{2})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{3}^{′}=f({x}_{3},{y}_{3})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{3},{y}_{3})=(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx).$\n\nNow, we have the following table of values:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |\n\nWith this in mind, let's find each point at which the slope is evaluated in turn using the values given in the table.\n\n- The slope ${y}^{′}$ is evaluated at the initial point $(x,y)=({x}_{0},{y}_{0})=(0,1).$\n\n- The estimated slope ${y}_{1}^{′}$ is evaluated at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{1},{y}_{1}) & =(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}\\cdot Δx) \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4},\\,1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The estimated slope ${y}_{2}^{′}$ is evaluated at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{2},{y}_{2}) & =(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\\cdot Δx) \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4},\\,1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The estimated slope ${y}_{3}^{′}$ is evaluated at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{3},{y}_{3}) & =(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx) \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{1}{4},\\,1+(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{3}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, of the given options, the slope is evaluated at the points \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327582/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9740440-bdfb-588e-8f23-2eec9427e449"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327582"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330277/field-1/45753729b7eea380690757236f1fd5b9e8d959b4cb54a7c77e8dd1b3c7b54c27" :answer/id #uuid "829d4ba3-5167-5bc9-b5fd-ef5f19c60f8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Δx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330277/field-1/d892a7ca3878476dafc8d1def6f0ad795357793bd2192147fe4018018d744b58" :answer/id #uuid "5bec9777-26e8-531c-bff2-95d63ced661f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+Δy)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330277/field-1/ed6a1f718571a57c493fbdc1693741310e9f98c70478f81ce9d583fb1b019e2e" :answer/id #uuid "dcb44e46-11c3-5a14-8915-eb4ae3f2f9d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+Δx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330277/field-1" :answer-