},{y}_{3})=(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx).$\n\nAll four sample slopes are already computed. So, we just need to find the increment on $y.$\n\nWe compute $Δy$ using the Runge-Kutta method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(1+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{13}{8}+\\frac{37}{16})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot \\frac{153}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{51}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed first row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{13}{8}$ | $\\frac{37}{16}$ | $\\frac{51}{64}$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+\\frac{51}{64} \\\\  & =\\frac{115}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these rows to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{13}{8}$ | $\\frac{37}{16}$ | $\\frac{51}{64}$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{115}{64}$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈\\frac{115}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-339800/field-1/2ee71f97da76a36a5f98bee4ae2425715bbc4597486731aaed28becb23704cce" :answer/id #uuid "53b58a2a-5a50-59f5-bbb3-edb5517ed905" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339800/field-1/36bd4767b4dcb6cbfe49e6bf46e014bd92e359a1fadf3fe464658fcbf70d048e" :answer/id #uuid "d391cecb-ed