c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339813/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "600e9728-3ee3-53c9-8bee-016ff205c3bd" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339813/field-3/471d022dc8477dee5b5835181abb5643fcc83818c373aaad08fa968767db722e" :answer-field/choices ["q-339813/field-3/cb69a2cee94d066e797c8817f9478c282b4df4f9410863e07a754e6c3274ab5c" "q-339813/field-3/34219f229a95b374101226ed6e8380124ab0bbcf04f479caa9d1b203ca15969e" "q-339813/field-3/471d022dc8477dee5b5835181abb5643fcc83818c373aaad08fa968767db722e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339813/field-4/99e2b5754349f37ea380857308f6291cb13b27c6d7da23f5f1905ba4bf86e8c5" :answer/id #uuid "ff8db8b9-7653-5525-aeb9-05d9ba42aab9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339813/field-4/2c58a35088f686a92f272ff96f87810f98ad35f6c40e42c6cfc62c5c5afa1288" :answer/id #uuid "d9d2deb8-0b55-5038-a3b7-148548a958b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339813/field-4/fee4336cfa8a8e3de84543d8a2c3898bb04d0ae1435dfb2fe94980017e543934" :answer/id #uuid "5172abed-c7bf-57ef-b6b2-487598b03311" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339813/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd13adfc-7768-5ce4-be4b-605f2ee603cb" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339813/field-4/99e2b5754349f37ea380857308f6291cb13b27c6d7da23f5f1905ba4bf86e8c5" :answer-field/choices ["q-339813/field-4/99e2b5754349f37ea380857308f6291cb13b27c6d7da23f5f1905ba4bf86e8c5" "q-339813/field-4/2c58a35088f686a92f272ff96f87810f98ad35f6c40e42c6cfc62c5c5afa1288" "q-339813/field-4/fee4336cfa8a8e3de84543d8a2c3898bb04d0ae1435dfb2fe94980017e543934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339813" :question/id #uuid "1e447679-2e6d-5f49-8605-8ad19a8a2c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-339813" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2xy+{x}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method. Complete the table below, given that the step size is $Δx=1.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| $1$ | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c\n$$\n\nthe increment in $y$ using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method with step size $Δx$ is computed as the weighted average of four sample slopes:\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{′}=f(x,y)$ is the estimated slope at the initial point $(x,y),$\n\n- ${y}_{1}^{′}=f({x}_{1},{y}_{1})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{2}^{′}=f({x}_{2},{y}_{2})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{3}^{′}=f({x}_{3},{y}_{3})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{3},{y}_{3})=(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx).$\n\nThe first two sample slopes, evaluated at the initial point and first intermediate point, are already computed. Now let's find the others.\n\n- The second intermediate point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,({x}_{2},{y}_{2}) & =(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\\cdot Δx) \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1,\\,1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{13}{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second intermediate slope is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & =2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+({x}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{13}{8}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | $\\frac{15}{8}$ |  |  |\n\n- The third intermediate point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{3},{y}_{3}) & =(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx) \\\\  & =(0+1,\\,1+\\frac{15}{8}\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =(1,\\frac{23}{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the third intermediate slope is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{3}^{′} & =2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}+({x}_{3})^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot \\frac{23}{8}+{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | $\\frac{15}{8}$ | $\\frac{27}{4}$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using the Runge-Kutta Method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}+2\\cdot \\frac{15}{8}+\\frac{27}{4})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 13 \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed first row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | $\\frac{15}{8}$ | $\\frac{27}{4}$ | $\\frac{13}{6}$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+\\frac{13}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these rows to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | $\\frac{15}{8}$ | $\\frac{27}{4}$ | $\\frac{13}{6}$ |\n| $1$ | $\\frac{19}{6}$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1)≈\\frac{19}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339813/field-1" "q-339813/field-2" "q-339813/field-3" "q-339813/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43ab4b4b-4462-50e5-ad14-fb31a502be7d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339813"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339820/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "3afa7dfd-c5df-5ec6-955a-1a26eb1ce687" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339820/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "08501f5f-85f4-5ccb-86cd-52a0cb5b8e89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339820/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "a5c73611-9221-50bc-900a-3af960da3349" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339820/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee5cd1a9-45c7-5146-b116-93eb93aad47a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339820/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-339820/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-339820/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-339820/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3398